\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A focus carries an exponential factor}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{A small displacement #{y} from an [equilibrium](fnip-0014)
satisfies, to first order, the linearization
#{\dot y=Df(x_{*})y} from [Jacobian](fnip-0034). When the eigenvalues are
#{\alpha\pm i\beta} with #{\beta\neq 0}, each coordinate of a
solution carries the factor #{e^{\alpha t}} and oscillates with
angular frequency #{\beta}. The displacement decays when #{\alpha}
is negative and grows when #{\alpha} is positive.}

\p{\citet{(1.1.7), §1.1, p. 9}{guckenheimer1983nonlinear}
is that real pair of solutions. The Hopf column of \ref{fnip-0005}
has one [focus](fnip-0035) of each kind.
\ref{fnip-0037} records the eigenvalues.}
